+<title>REAPER &mdash; WDS</title>
+<!-- Reaper_WDS.asp - Wireless > WDS (Reaper-native UI, native wave, 2026-10-31).
+     Replaces Advanced_WMode_Content.asp; same nvram, same apply. Per radio unit N:
+       wlN_mode_x       "0" AP only | "1" WDS only | "2" Hybrid (AP + WDS)
+       wlN_wdsapply_x   "1" = bridge only to the listed peers, "0" = any peer (lazy WDS)
+       wlN_wdslist      "<MAC<MAC..." at most 4 (stock limit)
+     Consumer: init-broadcom.c (mode_x 1 -> wlN_mode=wds; wdsapply_x 1 -> wlN_wds = the list, lazywds 0; else
+     wds "", lazywds 1; mode_x 0 -> no WDS) -> wlconf/driver (closed). Apply = /applyapp.cgi with rc_service
+     restart_wireless (stock), only changed keys. Differences from stock, on purpose: every radio on one page (stock
+     cycled the global wl_unit); wlN_bw / channel / chanspec / nmode_x are NOT posted back (stock re-sent stale
+     copies of Wireless Settings' values); the peer picker uses Reaper's site survey (reaper_wifi.cgi svystart /
+     svydata - every radio incl. 6 GHz; stock used the prebuilt wl_scan_* handlers with no 6 GHz variant) and runs
+     only when asked (stock scanned on page load); MACs upper-cased; the long ASUS help text gave way to a short
+     note. A band the router uses as its repeater uplink is not editable (stock). -->
+<link rel="stylesheet" href="/reaper/rp.css">
+<style>
